      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "For most homeowners in Utah, a complete roof replacement costs between $8,500 and $19,500. The average price for a standard 2,000-square-foot home typically lands right around $14,800 for a full tear-off and installation of standard architectural shingles.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "between $8,500 and $19,500"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Depending on your specific goals, the ultimate price tag is determined by two main factors: your home's total square footage and the material you choose."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Cost by Home Size (Standard Asphalt Shingles)"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "The layout of your home affects the overall roof surface area (which includes pitch and overhangs). Here is a general breakdown of typical pricing across the state:"
      },
